# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   Documented here: https://github.com/pyenv/pyenv#local-version-file
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if you want to keep lock files out:
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Using Poetry, it's common to commit poetry.lock but exclude the virtual environment
#   .venv is handled in "Environments" below.

